## NINEONELABS Renewal Project — Responsive Design System Report

### Breakpoint System & Container Sizes

**Breakpoints (Mobile-First via `mq()` mixin):**
- `xs`: 375px
- `sm`: 544px
- `md`: 768px (mobile/tablet threshold)
- `lg`: 1024px
- `xl`: 1440px (desktop standard)
- `2xl`: 1640px
- `3xl`: 1920px

### Mixin Signature & Usage

**Core mixin signature:**
```scss
@mixin mq($key-or-size, $direction: "max") {
  @if (meta.type-of($key-or-size) == "string") {
    $size: map.get(var.$containers, $key-or-size);
    @media (#{$direction}-width: #{$size}px) {
      @content;
    }
  } @else if (meta.type-of($key-or-size) == "number") {
    @media (#{$direction}-width: #{$key-or-size}px) {
      @content;
    }
  }
}
```

**Convenience wrappers:**
- `@include mq(md)` → `@media (max-width: 768px)` (mobile-first downward)
- `@include mq-min(lg)` → `@media (min-width: 1024px)` (for upward breakpoints)
- `@include mq-max(md)` → explicit max-width

**Location:** `/resource/scss/abstract/_mixins.scss` (lines 12–26)

### ResponsiveRuntime — isMobile Definition

**File:** `/resource/ts/runtime/ResponsiveRuntime.ts`

**Breakpoint resolution (line 134–139):**
```typescript
private _resolveBreakpoint(viewportWidth: number): ResponsiveBreakpoint {
  if (viewportWidth < 768) return "mobile";      // < md
  if (viewportWidth < 1024) return "tablet";     // < lg
  if (viewportWidth < 1600) return "desktop";    // < 1600
  return "wide";                                  // >= 1600
}
```

**isMobile flag:** Sourced from `Device.isMobile` (device-based detection), then snapshot includes:
- `isMobile: device.isMobile` (line 90)
- CSS variables applied: `--r-breakpoint`, `--rvw`, `--rvh`, `--rdpr`, `--r-viewport-scale`, etc. (lines 173–182)

### Fluid Spacing & Typography System

**Fluid values use `fluid()` function** (not viewport units directly):
- Example: `padding: fluid(24, 48)` scales between 24px and 48px based on viewport width
- Applied across gutter tokens: `var(--gutter-xs)` through `var(--gutter-4xl)`

**Gutter map (fluid min/max pairs):**
```scss
$gutters: (
  3xs: (min: 4, max: 6),
  xs: (min: 10, max: 14),
  sm: (min: 14, max: 20),
  md: (min: 20, max: 28),
  lg: (min: 28, max: 40),
  xl: (min: 36, max: 52),
  2xl: (min: 48, max: 96),
  3xl: (min: 96, max: 160),
  4xl: (min: 128, max: 220),
);
```

### Concrete Responsive Patterns (from _sub.scss and _main.scss)

**Pattern 1: Works Gallery — Layout Shift (lines 1580–1646 in _sub.scss)**
```scss
.no-sub-works {
  &__inner {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 3fr 9fr;  // Desktop: sidebar + content
    gap: var(--gutter-md);
  }

  @include mq(md) {
    &__inner {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;    // Tablet: stacked
    }
    &__filter {
      position: static;              // Unsticky on mobile
      height: auto;
    }
    &__gallery-list {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);  // 2-column grid
      gap: var(--gutter-md) var(--gutter-sm);
    }
  }

  @include mq(sm) {
    &__gallery-list {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;   // Single column
    }
    &__filter {
      display: none;                 // Hide sidebar filter
    }
    &__gallery-mobile-filter {
      display: block;                // Show mobile filter sheet
    }
  }
}
```

**Pattern 2: Services Grid — Reflow (lines 817–833 in _main.scss and lines 603–619 in _sub.scss)**
```scss
&__item {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 2fr 6fr 4fr;  // Desktop: 3-column
  gap: var(--gutter-sm);
  align-items: center;
  padding: var(--gutter-2xl) 0;

  @include mq(md) {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;  // Tablet+Mobile: single column
    gap: var(--gutter-xs);
  }
}
```

**Pattern 3: Main Intro — Width Shift + Alignment (lines 76–189 in _main.scss)**
```scss
.no-main-intro-1 {
  width: 50% !important;          // Desktop: half width
  margin-right: auto;

  @include mq(lg) {
    width: 70% !important;        // Large tablet
  }

  @include mq(md) {
    width: 100% !important;       // Mobile: full width
  }
}

&__txt--top {
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-end;

  @include mq(md) {
    align-items: flex-start;      // Alignment shift at md
  }
}
```

**Pattern 4: Client Grid — Column Count + Gap Reduction (lines 1027–1098 in _main.scss)**
```scss
&__items {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);  // Desktop: 2-column
  gap: var(--gutter-md);
}

@include mq(md) {
  &__items {
    gap: var(--gutter-sm);  // Tighter spacing on smaller screens
  }
}
```

### Fluid vs. Fixed Values Strategy

The system uses:
1. **Fluid values** for responsive spacing: `fluid(min, max)` scales continuously
2. **Token-based gutters**: `var(--gutter-*)` for consistent gaps
3. **Breakpoint-based reflow**: `@include mq()` for layout structure changes (grid columns, display modes)
4. **Full-width content at `sm`**: Forms typically show as single-column modal/sheet on phones

All files use `@use "../abstract" as *` to import the mixin and variable system centrally.

